kexts/NVRMFB, tools  The retry of a head that does not light at power-on (NVRMFB's setPowerState(1) queues the GPU
             wake call, which tries again) and the kernel log lines for the branch a power-on takes and for the length
             of a system wake's DidWake(false) replay come from pull request 597 by Geek to the original project
             (https://github.com/nullmoth/nvidia-macos-driver), adapted here: each retry is queued 500 ms later, at
             most three attempts in one wake, instead of waited for under the display gate, and the reordering of the
             system wake's notifications is not taken. tools/test_display_power_retry.py carries that pull request's
             addition to the test, changed for the delay. kexts/NVRMFB and tools/ are under PolyForm Noncommercial
             1.0.0 like this project (LICENSE).

